# Accepted gitleaks findings, one line per FINDING (commit:file:rule:line), never a path pattern.
#
# A path-level exemption is a standing blind spot exactly where fixtures and configs concentrate —
# it exempts every file the directory will ever contain, including ones nobody has written yet. Each
# entry below therefore names one exact finding and carries the reason it is accepted. An entry that
# stops matching anything is unaccounted-for permission: delete it in the change that made it stale.
#
# This file was created from the triage that armed the scanner (gitleaks 8.30.1 over all 241 commits
# of history, 2026-08-24). Exactly one finding, and it is a false positive; the repository has never
# committed a credential, which is why there is no baseline file and why CI gates on zero.
#
# NOTE FOR FUTURE ENTRIES: do not quote the flagged text here. This file is scanned like every other
# file in the tree (deliberately — an allowlist is a fine place to hide a secret), so a rationale
# that reproduces the finding verbatim re-trips the rule on itself, forever, one commit later.
# Describe the finding; the fingerprint already identifies it exactly.

# `generic-api-key`, an entropy hit on a test assertion message about a minimum-cost floor. The line
# declares a numeric threshold and happens to sit next to a variable whose name is three letters
# long and begins with k; there is no credential in it, and the line has since moved. Kept as a
# fingerprint (not a file exemption) so tests_ingest.rs stays fully scanned.
78b4869d5390a42246e491fa659ef066563a41e6:crates/api/src/tests_ingest.rs:generic-api-key:903

# The same false positive, quoted verbatim inside this file's own rationale by the commit that
